{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01PD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Spec(R) \\subset X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{A} = \\widetilde{A}$", "MATH_0006": "$A$", "MATH_0007": "$R$", "MATH_0008": "$R$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:074452414bfcd575b536b9737bfe1bbddf0ded3e9aaafcaa6252ef310f7dba57", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4871ba2544a81b208d56255f564b07d655da7859c1e516b44d374a8dd3e01d8a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme. In the following lemma we use the notion\nof a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>quasi-coherent <MATH_0002>-algebra <MATH_0003>\nof finite type<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>. This means that for every affine open\n<MATH_0004> we have <MATH_0005>\nwhere <MATH_0006> is a (commutative) <MATH_0007>-algebra which is of finite type\nas an <MATH_0008>-algebra.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b1d16c788d4db2f1a34a65553ed25a7e3592b22af5d59a6ec0a0b3c138e3974e", "unit_id": "tag:01PD:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01PD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-algebra-directed-colimit-finite-type}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:993af4ce99c00ad75d81fd44f0d0794849ce83069498b3d8e1447f02c5024bbb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d6a7ef12fafcc136f8fb0cde3563894014df98b0e5b038dece2138a23b57e7c7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Assume <MATH_0002> is quasi-compact and quasi-separated.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a quasi-coherent <MATH_0004>-algebra.\nThen <MATH_0005> is the directed colimit of its finite type\nquasi-coherent <MATH_0006>-subalgebras.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f5796db25ab126d7d82e73d07e4ed4fd10278ace45817ae47f88fc5a6127eab5", "unit_id": "tag:05JT:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01PD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{A}_1, \\mathcal{A}_2 \\subset \\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{A}_1 \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_X} \\mathcal{A}_2 \\to \\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{A}_1$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{A}_2$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{A} = \\colim_i \\mathcal{A}_i$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{A}'_i = \\Im(\\mathcal{A}_i \\to \\mathcal{A})$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-algebra-directed-colimit-finite-presentation}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:94af75d99d8711235553ab585e0811a8196db09c049636107bca92675e1bb859", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4587773e89d66e4e4ab0f882c9b2e52c0c5ecbdf66399fb7a95984665a5d9fda", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> are\nquasi-coherent <MATH_0002>-subalgebras of finite type, then the image of\n<MATH_0003>\nis also a quasi-coherent <MATH_0004>-subalgebra of finite type\n(some details omitted) which contains both <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006>.\nIn this way we see that the system is directed.\nTo show that <MATH_0007> is the colimit of this system, write\n<MATH_0008> as a directed\ncolimit of finitely presented quasi-coherent <MATH_0009>-algebras as in\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nThen the images <MATH_0010> are\nquasi-coherent subalgebras of <MATH_0011> of finite type. Since\n<MATH_0012> is the colimit of these the result follows.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f8261b2b920153187f12de28a2a27bb9808cd4a4e32dc17836805f028c9eb2a2", "unit_id": "tag:05JT:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01PD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Spec(R) \\subset X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{A} = \\widetilde{A}$", "MATH_0006": "$A$", "MATH_0007": "$R$", "MATH_0008": "$R$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ ", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:074452414bfcd575b536b9737bfe1bbddf0ded3e9aaafcaa6252ef310f7dba57", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0bab31c30728ba8072b8dbe34b172b12d1a3f2f89de9d5a7cd47c2d8cc2551f3", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme. In the following lemma we use the notion\nof a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>finite (resp.<SPACE_0001>integral) quasi-coherent\n<MATH_0002>-algebra <MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>. This means that for every\naffine open <MATH_0004> we have\n<MATH_0005> where <MATH_0006> is a (commutative) <MATH_0007>-algebra\nwhich is finite (resp.<SPACE_0002>integral) as an <MATH_0008>-algebra.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e2092ae7f41961a1304ea595c7b48666b8e48e0d8c7fa305a82e750483314f96", "unit_id": "tag:01PD:prose-0005"}
